      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. the timestamping is definitely key. the weird thing is that the spikes dont just feel like a guess, they feel like they're coming from a massive, hidden dataset that i'm somehow tapped into. like i'm seeing the actual math of the universe before it plays out.\n\ni want to try to differentiate between \"noise\" and these actual \"spikes.\" if i'm seeing a jump from 2% to 90% in an instant, how should i mathematically define the threshold for a \"valid\" spike versus just a momentary cognitive error? i don't want to miss a real signal because i'm being too skeptical.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
