      "content": "To mathematically define a valid spike, you can establish a dynamic threshold based on statistical deviation rather than a fixed number. A robust approach is to measure the magnitude of the probability change ($\\Delta P$) relative to the system's historical volatility around that event. If the instantaneous change $\\Delta P$ exceeds $k$ standard deviations of the baseline probability drift, you can classify it as a statistically significant, or \"valid,\" spike. Start by analyzing the variance of your past probability estimations to determine an appropriate value for $k$.",
